You Mean him do you look nothing alike?

11
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,296
I'm off to practice.

12
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,151
I'll see you later, okay?

13
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,320
Good morning. Sugu?

14
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,460
God, seriously?

15
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:54,337
Instead of lurking, you
should have said something!

16
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:58,260
Yeah, well, you were practicing
and I didn't want to bother you.

17
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,240
I wasn't really practicing.

18
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,540
I guess it's just habit is all.

19
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:06,577
Oh, hmm.

20
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:08,719
At least you've been keeping it up.

21
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:10,917
It's light.

22
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,397
what it's not light it's timber

23
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:18,057
bamboo oh yeah right I meant

24
00:05:18,140 --> 00:05:22,717
like it's lighter than I thought
it's not as heavy as what

25
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:29,217
I'm used to what the heck's

26
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:34,357
he comparing it to you hey you

27
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:37,969
think maybe we could give it a
go what you mean a match like

28
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:41,797
seriously? Yep.

29
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,757
A real match with pads and stuff?

30
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,620
Yeah, on second thought, no

31
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:47,790
contact.

32
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,877
I mean, I'd feel like crap
if I ended up hurting you.

33
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,380
I still gotta dig out grandpa's old gear.

34
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,485
How about we spar in the dojo?

35
00:05:55,740 --> 00:06:00,860
Whoa, you sound pretty darn confident for
someone who's been asleep for two years.

36
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,920
For your information, I

37
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:07,097
was a quarter-finalist in
the middle school nationals.

38
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:10,297
Seriously though, are you sure
you're feeling up to this?

39
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:12,204
You might want to take it easy.

40
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:19,767
I've been doing rehab in the gym every
day, so I think I'm gonna be good to go.

41
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:35,780
What kind of stance is
that supposed to be?

42
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,620
Don't you worry about it.

43
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:39,360
This is my own style.

44
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:43,160
Okay. Ready? Uh-huh.

45
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,840
His head's wide open.

46
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,900
That'll be my first strike.

47
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:54,470
Huh?

48
00:06:54,553 --> 00:06:57,580
It's an odd stance, but he looks composed.

49
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,480
Okay then.

50
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:36,620
Oh my god, are you okay?

51
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,320
Okay, okay, you win.

52
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,420
You sure are strong, Sugu.

53
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:45,958
You'd mop the floor with Heathcliff.

54
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:49,540
Maybe you should sit down
or something. I'm good.

55
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,415
Thanks for the match.

56
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,457
Did I hit you too hard?

57
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,417
No, I'm okay.

58
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,897
Just years of habit.

59
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:14,417
Let's see—my footwork was
okay, but the attacks sucked!

60
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:19,117
I guess I can't use the sword skills I
acquired unless I got the system helping.

61
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,729
helping I have to say
I'm really surprised.

62
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:24,897
I mean, how long have you been
practicing behind my back?

63
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:30,020
Oh, you know, it is kind of fun
after all, but you never know.

64
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,537
Maybe I'll take it up again.

65
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:32,450
Really?

66
00:08:32,533 --> 00:08:34,500
Oh, seriously? Yeah, sure.

67
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,337
You want to be my teacher?

68
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,250
Are you kidding?

69
00:08:37,333 --> 00:08:38,163
Of course.

70
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:40,516
We'll train together like we used to.

71
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,360
After I build up some more muscle, okay?

72
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,440
I've been practicing, too.

73
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,359
Want to know what?

74
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,430
Huh?

75
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,040
Nope, I'll keep it a secret.

76
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,860
That is so not cool.

77
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:02,780
You going anywhere today? Oh.

78
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,980
I don't know.

79
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,557
I guess...

80
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:07,760
the hospital?

81
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,960
Oh, you are?

82
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:15,610
That's nice.

83
00:09:15,693 --> 00:09:17,397
Her name's Asuna, right?

84
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,540
You visit her a lot.

85
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,130
Uh-huh.

86
00:09:22,213 --> 00:09:23,043
As much as I can.

87
00:09:23,126 --> 00:09:25,176
It's the only thing I can do for her.

88
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:29,800
Anyway, Sugu, it's my turn
to make breakfast today.

89
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:32,797
It'll be ready by the time
you finish your shower.

90
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:33,710
Okay.

91
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,117
It's been two months
since I beat Heathcliff.

92
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:46,080
Two months since I beat The Death Game.

93
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:52,237
When I woke up, I talked to someone
from the Ministry of Internal Affairs.

94
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:55,277
I told them everything I knew about Sao,

95
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:59,180
and in exchange they
told me where Asuna was.

96
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:09,040
I found out she was nearby in Saitama.

97
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:13,332
Asuna's family admitted her
to Tokoazawa General Hospital.

98
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:18,900
I also found out that besides her,

99
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:23,000
there's about 300 other players
who haven't woken up yet.

100
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,857
Akihiko Kayaba's still missing,

101
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:34,077
and people think he's keeping
the players in their comas?

102
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:35,440
as part of his plan.

103
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:40,320
SAO isn't over, not by a long shot.

104
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:54,690
Asuna.

105
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,350
Kazuto.

106
00:11:05,433 --> 00:11:07,139
Sorry, I didn't know you were here.

107
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,715
Thank you for coming.

108
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,580
Hello, Mr. Yuki.

109
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,480
I hope it's okay I'm here.

110
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:15,480
Please, you can visit whenever you like.

111
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,460
I know it makes her happy.

112
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:25,650
Sir.

113
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:31,225
Oh, I don't think the
two of you have ever met.

114
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:32,460
This is Sugo.

115
00:11:32,780 --> 00:11:34,920
He's our company's director of R &D.

116
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:36,960
I'm Nobuyuki Sugo.

117
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:38,220
It's a pleasure.

118
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,160
I'm Kazuto Kirigaya.

119
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:43,960
You're THE Kirito?

120
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,097
You're a hero.

121
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:46,040
It's an honor.

122
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:48,160
Oh, I'm sorry.

123
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:52,497
I know we're not supposed to talk about
what happened inside the SAO server.

124
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:55,160
But he's my partner's son, so it's fine.

125
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:58,760
Besides, I've always thought
of him as part of my family.

126
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:03,380
Actually, sir, speaking of family,

127
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:07,320
if I may, I'd like to make it
official as soon as possible.

128
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:09,560
This is sudden.

129
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:12,477
Are you sure this is really what you want?

130
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,148
I mean, you're still young.

131
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:16,517
You have your whole life ahead of you.

132
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,718
Thank you for your concern,
but my heart's set on it.

133
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:25,033
It sounds strange, but even though
she's like this, she's still beautiful.

134
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:27,851
I'd like to see her in that wedding dress.

135
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:30,440
You have a point.

136
00:12:31,940 --> 00:12:35,646
The sooner we prepare ourselves
for the inevitable, the better.

137
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:40,738
Sorry to cut the conversation short.

138
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,508
I have a meeting to get to.

139
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,120
We can talk more about this later.

140
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:48,140
Kazuto, take care.

141
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:01,720
I heard you and Asuna
were lovers in the game.

142
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,020
Is that true?

143
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,230
Uh-huh.

144
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:06,796
That is unfortunate.

145
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:11,198
It's going to make for one complicated
relationship between you and I.

146
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:24,580
In case you're curious, her father and
I were discussing her marriage to me.

147
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:30,697
No way you can't do that?

148
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:33,437
You have a point; it's true.

149
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:37,177
We can't legally marry, but
if the Yuki family adopts me,

150
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:41,177
it'll be as if we are on paper—that
is just like we're married.

151
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:45,717
The truth is, she's always hated
me ever since we were kids;

152
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:50,737
neither my parents nor hers know that
if I proposed and she could speak,

153
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:53,137
I'm pretty sure her answer would be no.

154
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:57,777
For me, this situation is very favorable.

155
00:13:57,860 --> 00:14:00,897
Stop it!

156
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:01,810
Who

157
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,157
do you think you are?

158
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:10,017
You can't take advantage
of Asuna like this!

159
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:10,930
Take

160
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,130
advantage—oh, please!

161
00:14:12,213 --> 00:14:18,157
If anything, I have a right to
her; perhaps I should explain why?

162
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,120
explain why

163
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:22,960
Any idea what happened to Argus?

164
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,940
They're the company that developed SAO.

165
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:29,240
I heard they closed it down. Very good.

166
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:33,700
The lawsuits and damages they
had to pay took their toll.

167
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,394
The company was forced into bankruptcy.

168
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:41,000
But the maintenance of the SAO
servers was given to another company.

169
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:46,740
An electronics manufacturer, where
Asuna's father, Shozo Yuki, is the CEO.

170
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:48,780
Wrecked progress.

171
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,530
Yes.

172
00:14:50,613 --> 00:14:53,800
And I work for the company's Full
Dive Technology R &D division.

173
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,260
In other words,

174
00:14:56,460 --> 00:15:01,284
and without getting into specifics, you
could say I'm the one keeping Asuna alive.

175
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:06,685
Now I ask you, is it wrong for me to expect
a little compensation for my trouble?

176
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:11,377
I don't know what kind of promises
you made to each other in the game,

177
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:12,872
and I don't really care.

178
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:16,137
But I don't ever want
to see you here again.

179
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:17,050
Understood?

180
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:20,960
And from now on, stay
away from the Yuki family.

181
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:25,520
We're having the ceremony here
on January 26th, a week from now.

182
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:26,990
Save the date.

183
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:30,877
Even though you're not welcome here
anymore, you should come to the wedding.

184
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,240
No need to thank me.

185
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:35,740
Well, Mr.

186
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:38,566
Hero, you've got the
room all to yourself now.

187
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,400
Say goodbye and get out.

188
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:50,121
Kazuto, the bathroom's all yours!

189
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,680
Geez, what's wrong?

190
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:01,617
Why didn't you say something?

191
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:04,380
And turn on the heat,
it's freezing in here!

192
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:13,220
Sorry, I just want to be left alone.

193
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:16,148
Hey, how come you didn't
turn the heater on?

194
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,680
What's wrong? Are you okay?

195
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:21,020
Yeah, it's nothing.

196
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:23,620
Okay, but you're freezing.

197
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:25,949
You're gonna catch a cold.

198
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:28,920
I could run you a hot bath if you want.

199
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,880
I'm so hopeless and weak.

200
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:36,240
I didn't want you to see this.

201
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:40,385
I swore no matter what, you'd
never see me being such a crybaby.

202
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,520
Is it Asuna?

203
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:47,490
Is she okay?

204
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:50,307
Did something happen to her?

205
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:53,820
She's leaving.

206
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,320
Somewhere far away.

207
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,597
And I'll never...

208
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:00,800
I'm never gonna see her again.

209
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:21,300
Hey, hang in there, okay?

210
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:26,280
If you really love someone that
much, even when things look hopeless,

211
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,660
you can't give up.

212
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:34,440
I know I can't.

213
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:39,280
And I won't lie to myself anymore.

214
00:17:47,180 --> 00:17:49,680
Gosh, I remember it like it was yesterday.

215
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,897
Kazuto stood there looking at me,

216
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:56,737
and then he told me he wanted to
know who his real parents were.

217
00:17:56,820 --> 00:17:59,408
I was so shocked, I
didn't know what to say.

218
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,755
He was only ten, but here's the thing.

219
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:06,688
Somehow, he logged onto the Citizen's
Registration Network and found the file.

220
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:08,950
That figures.

221
00:18:09,033 --> 00:18:10,917
Sounds just like something he'd do.

222
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,235
I was so stunned, I couldn't
think of a way to deny it.

223
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:16,272
So what do I do instead?

224
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:20,117
I tell him how my big sister and
her husband are his real parents.

225
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,030
Wow.

226
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:26,540
Mom, I was wondering. About what?

227
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:30,457
I guess about the way he's
been since middle school.

228
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:33,697
He'd go into his room and
play games online for hours.

229
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:36,497
You think it's because he found
out about his real parents?

230
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:37,660
No, not at all.

231
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:40,437
He was always into
computers and technology.

232
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:44,777
By the time he was six, he'd already
built his own computer out of spare parts.

233
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:48,957
If anything, he's like that because
he's a huge computer nerd like me.

234
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,400
Or so he thinks.

235
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:55,228
Well, I'm heading home
and get dinner ready.

236
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:57,860
Don't stay too long, okay, Suguha?

237
00:18:58,460 --> 00:19:00,220
Don't worry. I won't.

238
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,960
Happy birthday, kiddo.

239
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:18,140
He's my cousin, not my big brother.

240
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,120
I still have a hard time believing it.

241
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:25,840
My big brother.

242
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:56,600
But, in the end, your heart.

243
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,980
In the end, your heart.

244
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:07,740
Belongs to her.

245
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,600
Come on.

246
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,057
Wake up, Sugu.

247
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,040
It's morning.

248
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,977
I said you gotta wake up now.

249
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:36,589
You're not gonna have time to
practice if you don't wake up.

250
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:44,380
Oh, hey. Morning.

251
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,020
Rise and shine.

252
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:57,160
Hiya, sleepy.

253
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:06,737
Um, I...

254
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:08,320
Oh, my God!

255
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:15,940
As weird as ever.

256
00:21:21,220 --> 00:21:22,980
Just hang in there, okay?

257
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:26,900
She's right.

258
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:28,600
Yeah, she's right.

259
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:47,420
What the hell?

260
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:03,380
Asuna

261
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:09,557
